    <string name="terminos_title">Terms and Conditions</string>
    <string name="terminos_uso">Terms and Conditions of Use</string>
    <string name="terminos_actualizacion">Last updated: June 2026</string>
    <string name="terms_1_title">1. Acceptance of the Terms</string>
    <string name="terms_1_body">By downloading, accessing or using the Jam! app (\"the App\"), you agree to be bound by these Terms and Conditions. If you do not agree, do not use the App.</string>
    <string name="terms_2_title">2. Description of the Service</string>
    <string name="terms_2_body">Jam! is a social platform that allows users to create and join temporary social events called \'Jams\'. Users can connect with nearby people, chat in groups and coordinate in-person meetups.</string>
    <string name="terms_3_title">3. User Accounts</string>
    <string name="terms_3_body">To use the App you must create an account by providing accurate information. You are responsible for keeping your credentials confidential. You must be at least 13 years old (or the minimum age in your country) to use the App.</string>
    <string name="terms_4_title">4. Free Plan and Support</string>
    <string name="terms_4_body">The free plan allows you to create and join up to 10 Jams per week, with a limit of 15 participants per Jam. Voluntary community support removes these restrictions and offers additional features such as up to 150 participants, no ads and priority access to the project\'s development.</string>
    <string name="terms_5_title">5. Donations</string>
    <string name="terms_5_body">Donations are voluntary and are made by purchasing support points within the App. By purchasing points, you will automatically gain access to enhanced features as a thank you. Donations are non-refundable.</string>
    <string name="terms_6_title">6. User-Generated Content</string>
    <string name="terms_6_body">You are responsible for the content you post. You must not post illegal, offensive, discriminatory content or content that infringes the rights of third parties. We reserve the right to remove content and/or suspend accounts that violate these terms.</string>
    <string name="terms_7_title">7. Privacy and Data</string>
    <string name="terms_7_body">The App collects personal data such as name, ID number, location and preferences. This data is stored securely on Firebase (Google Cloud). We do not share your data with third parties without your consent. You can request deletion of your data at any time at contacto@jam-app.com.</string>
    <string name="terms_8_title">8. Limitation of Liability</string>
    <string name="terms_8_body">Jam! is a social coordination platform. We are not responsible for incidents that occur during meetups organized through the App. Users interact at their own risk. We recommend meeting in public places and taking safety precautions.</string>
    <string name="terms_9_title">9. Cancellation and Account Deletion</string>
    <string name="terms_9_body">You can delete your account at any time from the Profile section. When you delete your account, your personal data will be removed from our servers. Jams you have created will remain registered without your personal information.</string>
    <string name="terms_10_title">10. Modifications</string>
    <string name="terms_10_body">We reserve the right to modify these terms at any time. Changes will be notified through the App. Continued use after the changes constitutes acceptance of the new terms.</string>
    <string name="terms_11_title">11. Contact</string>
    <string name="terms_11_body">For inquiries about these terms, contact us at: contacto@jam-app.com</string>

